From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmd: cedit: keep the expo after 'cedit run'

'cedit run' destroys the expo when the user picks "Save", so the
command that saves the choices,

    cedit run && cedit write_env

finds nothing loaded ("No expo loaded") and the choices are lost. The
same goes for write_fdt and write_cmos. Seen on the Lctech Pi F1C200s:
the settings file written after a save came out empty.

Keep the expo after a run and free it when 'cedit load' replaces it.

Signed-off-by: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
---
--- a/cmd/cedit.c
+++ b/cmd/cedit.c
@@ -62,6 +62,9 @@
 		return CMD_RET_FAILURE;
 	}
 
+	/* the previous expo stays loaded after 'cedit run'; drop it here */
+	if (cur_exp)
+		expo_destroy(cur_exp);
 	cur_exp = exp;
 
 	return 0;
@@ -287,9 +290,12 @@
 		log_err("Failed (err=%dE)\n", ret);
 		return CMD_RET_FAILURE;
 	}
-	expo_destroy(cur_exp);
-	cur_exp = NULL;
 
+	/*
+	 * Keep the expo: the user's choices live in it, and 'cedit write_env'
+	 * (or write_fdt / write_cmos) after a successful run is how they are
+	 * saved. The next 'cedit load' frees it.
+	 */
 	return 0;
 }
 
